From 7099aac55c08cd93507267fd4c43602628e04a30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:11:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iOS 10 (32-bit) userland bring-up: address layout, slide info
 v2, syscalls

With these, iOS 10.3.4 (iPhone 5, armv7s) launchd maps its shared cache,
initializes libSystem and runs until libdispatch's root queue setup
(needs kevent workqueues, not implemented). iOS 7 is unchanged (tested).
- Root has an armv7s cache: shared region 0x1A000000..0x40000000 and the
  main stack below it (iOS 10's 32-bit layout), detected after mountroot.
- Shared cache slide info version 2 (iOS 9/10 caches).
- Commpage: user/kernel page shift (0x24, 0x25, 0x37); left at 0, iOS 10
  malloc used 1-byte pages.
- fcntl F_ADDFILESIGS_RETURN (whole file reported signed; not enforced)
  and F_CHECK_LV.
- Syscalls: sysctlbyname (274; was sem_getvalue, which only returned
  ENOSYS), getentropy (500), abort_with_payload / terminate_with_payload
  (521/520: print the reason, then kill), table up to 530.
- sysctl hw.targettype (N41) and kern.minimalboot.
- Bring-up aids: rpi3_systrace=PID logs that process's failing syscalls
  to serial; vm_allocate failures are logged.
